--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. RTKLIB (demo5, rtklibexplorer/RTKLIB)
   Revision 75a2e56275485b21a67bd35bc94bbeb8936e1a74 (demo5 b34L)
   Copyright (c) 2007-2020, T. Takasu
   License: BSD 2-Clause (A below; also crates/s20-ppk/vendor/rtklib/license.txt)
   Included as source in crates/s20-ppk/vendor/rtklib and compiled into the PPK
   engine. Changes made for this project are listed in crates/s20-ppk/README.md.
   Some of its files carry the notices of other contributors (T. Suzuki,
   M. Bavaro, Daniel A. Cook, Jens Reimann, Avinab Malla), under the same
   license.

   RTKLIB's src/sofa.c is derived from SOFA, the International Astronomical
   Union's Standards Of Fundamental Astronomy software collection
   (Copyright (C) 2021, 2023 IAU SOFA Board, www.iausofa.org), under the SOFA
   Software License (E below). It is not the official SOFA software: RTKLIB joined a few
   SOFA routines into one file (epv00, s2pv, obl06, pfw06, ir, rz, cp, rx,
   rxp, rxpv, moon98), declared unmodified arguments and constant data const,
   renamed iauEpv00 and iauMoon98 and made the others static; this project
   renamed those static routines with an "rk" prefix in place of "iau", as the
   SOFA license asks of derived routines. The changes are described at the top
   of that file.

2. small_gicp (koide3/small_gicp)
   Copyright (c) 2024 Kenji Koide
   License: MIT (B below)
   Point preprocessing, the Gaussian voxel map and the VGICP linearisation are
   ports of its algorithms: crates/s20-geom/src/cloud.rs, voxelmap.rs, vgicp.rs,
   so3.rs.

3. Potree (potree/potree)
   Copyright (c) 2011-2020, Markus Schütz
   License: BSD 2-Clause (C below)
   The eye-dome lighting shader (crates/s20-gui/src/edl.wgsl) follows Potree's
   edl.fs, itself adapted from CloudCompare's qEDL by Christian Boucheny; the
   adaptive point size follows Potree's. Reading Potree 2.0 octrees
   (crates/s20-io/src/potree.rs) follows its OctreeLoader.js and
   DecoderWorker_brotli.js, and the preview chooses the octree's nodes as it does
   (crates/s20-gui/src/scene.rs).

4. PotreeConverter (potree/PotreeConverter)
   Copyright 2020 Markus Schütz
   License: BSD 2-Clause (D below)
   The Potree 2.0 octrees written next to the output clouds
   (crates/s20-io/src/potree.rs) follow its layout and method: the folder and
   files, the counting grid cut into chunks, nodes sampled bottom-up on a 128³
   grid, BROTLI nodes of Morton-coded positions and colours.

The Rust crates built into this product, and the fonts egui embeds, are listed
with their licenses in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt (generated from Cargo.lock by
cargo-about; mostly MIT and/or Apache-2.0). `s20 licenses` and Help > License in
the GUI show both files.

Projects consulted for ideas only, with none of their code included: GLIM and
gtsam_points (koide3), fact-rs, LIO-SAM, FAST-LIO2, ERASOR2, Removert,
MirrorSentinel.

